{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>and she could not</b> — two times in the Masorah: here and the other: ולא יכלה ארץ מגוריהם. Teaches that she made him a cave in the earth, and even beneath the ground they dug after him, because they knew that from there the redeemer would emerge. And this is: \"the land could not\" — and \"she could not\" — still more hiding." "<b>גומא</b> — three times in the Masorah: here; and the other: השולח בים צירים ובכלי גומא על פני המים — that even in the sea He sent a ציר (messenger), which is Pharaoh's daughter, to save כלי גומא; and the other in Job: היגאה גומא — alluding to the one who says Job lived in the days of Moses."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:43.838465553Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}